  "x-semantic-contract": {
    "scope": "Pure DTO consistency comparator/review-scope staging; database actor authorization, immutable manifest membership, sealed historical origin authentication and actual original PDF bytes remain repository loader responsibility. No claim of authentication from a caller-supplied hash.",
    "native": "Descriptor/exact-builtin guard before any property read/callback. Existing whole-input limits8M serialized UTF8 including escaping/punctuation,200knodes including keys,depth64,container32768,string2M codepoints. No callbacks/proxies/cycles/holes/customserializers/surrogates/floats/unsafe/nonfinite; violations INVALID_INPUT, limits INPUT_LIMIT. No truncation.",
    "collections": "sources<=64, origins<=128, claims<=16 per source and<=128 total. Distinct source IDs, distinct origin(sourceID,checkID), unique source stages. Every non-null review has paired non-null snapshot pointer. Empty scope allowed but unbound.",
    "keys": "Frozen lighting clean scalar key:1..200codepoints, no leading/trailing fixed Python whitespace or U0000..0008,U000A..001F,U2028,U2029,U+FFFD. CheckID/link120. Reference8..1000. Position literal exact source grammar token1..80.",
    "pageStages": "Canonical positive decimal safe-integer page keys1..16digits, within every retained original pageCount for that source; same stage semantics as full-v3 source consumer. Source stages must be exactly one PD or RD for each retained claim; every non-UNRESOLVED page override equals that stage. Effective selected stage must equal it; no inference.",
    "origins": "Validate EVERY retained origin before selecting requested identity, including unclaimed/unrelated. Exact source/object association; full readDocumentTextV3Artifact on original envelope, no facade. inputSHA/sourceID exact; textArtifactHash equals whole domain v3 content hash; textStageContentHash equals SHA256(portable canonical FULL artifact bytes). All3recorded v3 traversal profiles retained. Origins can belong to earlier source-audit run manifests; do not force origin manifest hash equal current comparison manifest, loader proves source membership.",
    "claims": "Validate EVERY retained claim and review association before requested scope selection. Review source/object/hash/decision/content exact pointer equality. Each target resolves exactly one origin(sourceFileId,checkId), all3 target hashes(manifest/stage/artifact) match origin. declarationSnapshot source/SHA/artifact/profile exact rebuilt output. Reconstruct full original using source stage, review pageStages, exact selection and compare entire declaration + standalone domain declarationContentHash. Stale/malformed output cannot be ignored because unrelated.",
    "selection": "Collect all reconstructed claims where entityKey equals requested entityKey OR buildingKey/systemKey/positionKey all equal requested identity tuple. Any selected differing full identity => POSITION_IDENTITY_CONFLICT. Per stage repeated declaration hash => INVALID_INPUT; >1PD or >1RD => AMBIGUOUS_DECLARATION_SCOPE; exactly1PD+1RD and different sourceFileIds AND different original sourceSha256 required, else MATCHED_DECLARATION_PAIR_UNVERIFIED.",
    "eligibility": "Selected pair review revisionCURRENT and approvalAPPROVED. PD section ZU or IOS1; RD section IOS1 or EOM. Both same nonempty linkGroupId. Both source-authored NAMED_POSITION_LITERAL and nonnull positionLabel; group declaration remains NAMED_POSITION_UNVERIFIED. Explicit HUMAN_ASSERTED_SAME_LUMINAIRE_LIGHT_SOURCE_POSITION and sourcePositionLabel exactly original literal on each side. Claim identity is the human-reviewed same building/system/position/component mapping; matching literal L1 or arbitrary entityKey alone does not satisfy it. No completeness assertion for a positive substitution. No independent approved-change requirement invented from trigger. Reuploading identical PDF bytes as separate PD/RD IDs is not a replacement: same original SHA pair fails MATCHED_DECLARATION_PAIR_UNVERIFIED at gate10, before review/predicate.",
    "predicate": "Only PD LED→RD FLUORESCENT or INCANDESCENT yields CANDIDATE. LED→LED, reverse pairs, other pairs all DIRECTED_TRANSITION_UNSUPPORTED; do not emit successful whole-parameter negative or inferred energy-efficiency rank. Source declared visibility/authority remain unverified in snapshots; no numerical probability is fabricated.",
    "gateOrder": [
      "1 native and total collection limits",
      "2 exact input/collections DTO shapes",
      "3 uniqueness/source/review/target associations",
      "4 all original envelopes and original hashes + pageStages actual bounds",
      "5 every claim source-stage consistency",
      "6 every claim full-source reconstruction and declaration hash",
      "7 selected identity conflicts",
      "8 per-stage repeated declaration hashes",
      "9 per-stage ambiguity",
      "10 exactly one different-source PD/RD pair",
      "11 current/approved selected reviews",
      "12 selected electrical sections",
      "13 same nonempty link scope",
      "14 named source positions on both sides",
      "15 exact explicit position mappings",
      "16 directed pair predicate"
    ],
    "scopeHelpers": "validateLightingTechnologyScopeRequest returns detached exact staging request or null, validates limits/shapes/unique target declaration hashes; does not authenticate origin. projectLightingTechnologyScopeDecision returns detached request or null after standalone declaration DTO hash/source/SHA/textArtifactHash target consistency and selection equals source pageNumber+original sourcePath/raw of all primaryFragments; all claims in one decision same source ID/SHA. Does not reconstruct a fake v3 artifact or authenticate original.",
    "compatibility": "NEW pure TS/PY modules and canonical/types only. Existing producer/source readers/v1..v8 profiles/registry/runtime/results unchanged. No coverage increase until separately versioned execution/admission/runtime. Real F0161 stays UNBOUND, no approved genuine RD pair exists.",
    "returns": "ABSTAIN exact schema/status/reasonCode/calibratedProbability:null; CANDIDATE exact schema literal rule/scope fields, identity detached, source/review/declaration hash references and literal expected/actual technologies. No WARNING/ERROR at unknown probability."
  },
